```





FOR THE LINUX VERSION ::

## Linux / WSL version

This project runs on Linux and WSL using Python 3.9.13.

### Requirements
Install the dependencies with:

```bash
python3 -m pip install numpy matplotlib scikit-learn tensorflow
```

If you want to display images directly in a desktop Linux session, you can also install an image viewer such as Eye of GNOME (`eog`) or use the default system viewer.

### Run the program

```bash
python3 main.py
```

### Output

The script trains a neural network on the Iris dataset and saves the graphs as PNG files instead of opening popup windows:

- `training_curves.png`
- `confusion_matrix.png`
- `roc_curves.png`

### View the images on Linux

You can open the generated images with:

```bash
xdg-open training_curves.png
xdg-open confusion_matrix.png
xdg-open roc_curves.png
```

On Ubuntu, you can also use: (preferably)

```bash
eog training_curves.png 
```

### Notes

- The Linux version uses a non-interactive Matplotlib backend, so it works without `tkinter`.
- If `xdg-open` does not work, make sure you are running in a graphical desktop session.
